                    SparringCandidate(text: "Everything's in your inbox inside the hour, kickoff call Monday at nine, and on day one your managers get logins plus a fifteen-minute walkthrough — badges scan by the 24th.", evalDelta: 0.5, techniqueTags: ["concrete-construal", "mutual-close-plan", "assumptive"], next: "end", rationale: "She asked what happens; you handed her a calendar she can forward to her floor. Concrete motion inside the hour is how a verbal yes from a speed buyer stays a yes."),
                    SparringCandidate(text: "You're going to love the rollout — teams your size are usually fully adopted by week two, and I'll send over a summary of everything we agreed sometime tomorrow.", evalDelta: 0.1, techniqueTags: ["social-proof", "summary-close"], next: "end", rationale: "Reassurance and a recap tomorrow, for a buyer who wanted logistics today. Nothing wrong with it; nothing moving in it either."),
                ]),
            ],
            endings: SparringEndings(
                close: SparringEnding(buyerLine: "Signed. Fieldline's rep is still 'checking with his manager' on my last question — that's the whole reason you won. See you Monday at nine.", debrief: "You sold her the way she buys: a real number on the first ask, terms traded like a peer, and urgency only when it was true. The moves that lose the design partner — the firm anchor, the honest deadline — were the whole game here. The buyer sets the key, not the technique's reputation."),
                stall: SparringEnding(buyerLine: "Send me the paperwork and I'll see what procurement does with it. If it clears before the freeze, you'll hear from me.", debrief: "She left without a no, which from this persona is a slow no. Every hedge and half-answer added friction for a buyer whose hidden criterion was speed — the deal didn't die, it just stopped being worth her energy to push."),
                walk:  SparringEnding(buyerLine: "I'm going with Fieldline. Their rep answered every question I asked in one sentence — that's the whole vendor review, honestly.", debrief: "She never punished the price; she punished the dance. Discovery questions, team check-ins, and 'let me get back to you' each told her that her time mattered less than your process — and the competitor quote she warned you about was the exit she took.")
