            endings: SparringEndings(
                close: SparringEnding(buyerLine: "Send the one-pager tonight — exactly those words, my numbers. And keep Thursday: I want the team pulling for this before the CTO ever sees it. You realize I just pitched myself, right? Don't let anyone tell you that's not closing.", debrief: "No deck sent, no order form drafted — and the deal is further along than paper could put it during a freeze. He said the current state, the cost, and the future state in his own words, which is the entire job: a gap the buyer builds himself is the only one that survives a CTO's first question and a two-quarter freeze."),
                stall: SparringEnding(buyerLine: "This was genuinely great. Let's do the team demo when things calm down, and ping me after the round closes — I mean it, this isn't a brush-off.", debrief: "It isn't a brush-off — it's worse, because he means it. You got Problem answers and stopped digging, so the gap stayed sized in your head instead of his. A champion who can't say the cost out loud has nothing to fight the freeze with, and frozen quarters bury sincere intentions."),
                walk:  SparringEnding(buyerLine: "We're going to let the infra team take a swing at it in-house — honestly, the demo gave them ideas, which I guess is ironic. Genuinely appreciated the time.", debrief: "The demo taught his team just enough to build the pitch against you. Every turn spent showing features was a turn not spent making the cost of the status quo his — and a buyer who never says the number out loud can always afford to try the free version of you.")
